    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0460" n="1294" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/724</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-09T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 9, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4446. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 2032. Your 1774, Department’s 3225, December 4, 8 p.m. I note as per last
                    paragraph that you are sending copies of letters to the British and French
                    Embassies which furnish details with reference to American participation in the
                    purchase of molybdenum from Norway and iron ore from Sweden. In your 1502,
                    Department’s 2440, October 25 [<hi rendition="#italic">26</hi>], last sentence,
                    you stated that you were preparing a plan for handling resales of Swedish ore
                    which you would submit to me shortly. I have never received this and pending its
                    arrival I have never executed any agreement authorized in your 1444,
                    Department’s 2079 [<hi rendition="#italic">2279</hi>], October 18. If the
                    letters exchanged between you and the British and French Embassies have not
                    concretely covered our engagement concerning the purchase of Swedish ores and
                    the plan for handling resales, please send me the plan for resales mentioned in
                    your 1502 so that the whole matter may be arranged without further delay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
